<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Dutch Angola</h1><p class="st-meta">1641 CE – 1648 CE · capital Luanda</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Dutch West India Company's brief occupation of Luanda, which allied with Queen Njinga before Portugal retook the city in 1648.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>–Portuguese war, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company">Dutch West India Company</a> fleet under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cornelis-jol">Cornelis Jol</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luanda">Luanda</a> in August 1641, aiming to secure enslaved labour for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> plantations of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dutch-brazil">Dutch Brazil</a>. The Portuguese withdrew inland to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/massangano">Massangano</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwanza-river">Kwanza</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luanda">Luanda</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benguela">Benguela</a>, strengthened the fort they called Aardenburgh and shipped captives to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-republic-brazil">Brazil</a>. They allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/njinga-of-ndongo-and-matamba">Njinga Mbande</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-matamba">Kingdom of Matamba</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kingdom of Kongo</a> against the Portuguese, and their combined forces won victories in the interior, though they failed to destroy the Portuguese garrison at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/massangano">Massangano</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In August 1648 a fleet from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador-correia-de-sa-e-benevides">Salvador Correia de Sa</a> recaptured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luanda">Luanda</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> surrendered. The episode left <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/portuguese-angola">Portuguese Angola</a> restored and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/njinga-of-ndongo-and-matamba">Njinga</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo</a> exposed to Portuguese reprisals.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/dutch-angola.jpg" alt="Dutch Angola" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Flag_of_the_Dutch_West_India_Company.png: *Flag_of_the_Netherlands.svg: Zscout370 derivative work: Fentener van Vliss... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Dutch_West_India_Company.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1641 CE – 1648 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Luanda</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Dutch Reformed Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/angola">Angola</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dutch Loango-Angola, Fort Aardenburgh</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1644&amp;focus=dutch-angola" aria-label="Dutch Angola on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5046 2508 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Dutch Angola lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5366 2764L5366 2764M5366 2764L5097 634M5366 2764L5097 634"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5366 2764h0M5097 634h0M5097 634h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5366 2764h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5366 2764h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Luanda. <a href="/atlas?year=1644&amp;focus=dutch-angola">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

